{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And of Zebulun he said.</b> These are the five tribes that he blessed last — Zebulun, Gad, Dan, Naphtali, and Asher — and he doubled their names to strengthen them and make them mighty, because they were the weakest of all the tribes. These are the very ones that Joseph brought before Pharaoh, as it says (Genesis 47), ״וּמִקְצֵה אֶחָיו לָקַח חֲמִשָּׁה אֲנָשִׁים,״ because they looked weak, so that he would not appoint them as officers of his army." "<b>Rejoice, Zebulun, in your going out, and Issachar, in your tents.</b> Zebulun and Issachar made a partnership: Zebulun dwells by the seashore and goes out for trade in ships and earns, and gives into the mouth of Issachar, and they sit and engage in Torah. Therefore he put Zebulun before Issachar — because Issachar's Torah was through Zebulun (Bereshit Rabbah 99)." "<b>Rejoice, Zebulun, in your going out.</b> Succeed in your going out for merchandise." "<b>And Issachar.</b> Succeed in your sitting in tents for Torah — to sit and to intercalate years and to fix months, as it says (I Chronicles 12), ״וּמִבְנֵי יִשָּׂשכָר יוֹדְעֵי בִינָה לָעִתִּים… רָאשֵׁיהֶם מָאתָיִם״ — heads of the Sanhedrin who engaged in this, and by the fixing of their times and their intercalations —"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:48.975078145Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}